    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d333-a1">

                <pb facs="0353" n="347" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg347"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Weil to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New Orleans, La.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic">September 20,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: The Bluff Improvement Land Company
                    handed a protest to Minister Baker while in Bluefields in April last.</p>
                <p>The protest was against the Nicaraguan authorities expropriating said company’s
                    property.</p>
                <p>Kindly let me know what action has been taken in the matter and what the result
                    may be.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sam’l Weil</hi></signed>,<lb/>(For Bluff
                    Improvement Land Company, of Bluefields, Nicaragua.)</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
